# The key BPI release tags are signed with.
#
# This is NOT the test key beside it. test-key.pem signs the conformance
# vectors and its private half is published on purpose so the vectors can be
# regenerated; it proves nothing about who wrote anything. This file is the
# other thing: the public half of the key that signs release tags, so anyone
# can verify a tag came from the editor without trusting GitHub's badge.
#
# Verify a tag with:
#
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile conformance/keys/allowed-signers
#   git tag -v v0.2.0-draft
#
